  "notes": [
    "Blinded DEVELOPMENT corpus v1. Synthetic/staff-authored/generated/fallback text only; contains no real pilot data. Immutable: corrections publish a new artifact version. Reported separately from any future real held-out corpus (WP12b) — corpus_kind=development forever, and development metrics never stand in for human-gold validation."
  ],
  "body": {
    "corpus_kind": "development",
    "blinding_policy": "Staff-authored gold was written against the rubric text before inspecting coder output; synthetic and generated cases were authored from the rubric only. Evaluators run expected-vs-actual with case order shuffled by the runner; reviewers must not read actual coder output before signing off expected labels.",
    "unavoidable_unmasking": [
      "Authorship tags (synthetic/staff_authored/generated/fallback) and the adversarial flag are visible in the artifact — blinded scoring masks them at evaluation time, but the corpus file itself is not blinded.",
      "The deterministic coder is rules-based, so corpus cases necessarily resemble rubric examples; residual leakage is documented rather than eliminated — real held-out human gold (WP12b) remains the binding validation.",
      "Case ids encode the phenomenon under test (e.g. dev.negated_arrival); scorers treat ids as opaque during review."
    ],
    "cases": [
